# Adversarial case, ratified by the author 2026-08-04 (panel 015).
# Guards §4.4's own argument for why the type is
# mandatory on a mutable declaration. `totl @ total + x` reads the typo on the
# very line that writes it, so no unused rule could ever catch it: the only
# thing that makes it loud is that `@` writes to a name that must already be
# declared. If mutation ever declares, this file compiles and returns 0.
sum = function: (xs: [int]) -> int
    total: int @ 0
    for x in xs
        totl @ total + x
    return total
